         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Let Us Append\n\nAs with Hindu-Arabic numbers, when we move to the hundreds in Etruscan-Roman numbers, we add symbols in front of the tens and the units. Everything we learned before still applies.\n\nThe difference is that we are going to use a new group of symbols (C, D and M), instead of only reusing the previous symbols (I, V, X and L) in different positions.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "15d56b7c-e358-47c3-aef8-ee1de5602fae",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "15d56b7c-e358-47c3-aef8-ee1de5602fae",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "07666919-8290-4aee-a9fd-af148508f754",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=07666919-8290-4aee-a9fd-af148508f754",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
