            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "5fc193f7-7226-4852-82d1-706a44de71ec",
               "text": "The Missing Numbers",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=d603e3a0-cf2a-497d-9fc3-cfed73743515",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Welcome, New Old Logic\n\nTo use the bar, we take the numbers we have already learned and draw a bar on top of them. The bar shows that they represent thousands.\n\nThe table below repeats the Etruscan-Roman and Hindu-Arabic numbers, with four columns per line.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p data-custom=\"hundreds-and-thousands-table-thousands-bars\"></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "*Table 3: Numbers with a bar on top are read in thousands: 1000 to 9000.*",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
